meta {
  name: apply.list
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/sites/{{site}}/apply
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "action": "apply.list",
    "params": { "apply_id": "{{applyId}}" }
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  applyId: replace-with-an-apply-id
}

docs {
  # The steps one earlier write made

  Every write through the Apply door carries an `apply_id` and answers it back. `apply.list`
  takes that id and lists the steps it made (on WordPress each step is
  `{op, created, kind, id, key}`), which is how to tell whether a write landed.

  Set `applyId` in this request's Vars tab to an id a write answered. With a made-up id the
  component answers that it knows no such apply.

  This is a read, but it needs the `content` toolset: a seat without it gets
  `403 TOOLSET_NOT_GRANTED`.
}
